{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":[{"text":"Web search results for query: \"git-bug entity dag framework used for Bug Identity Board entities \"entity\" package what else\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Release 0.8.0 · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases/tag/v0.8.0\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/entity/dag/example_test.go at master · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/entity/dag/example_test.go\"},{\"title\":\"Pull requests · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/pulls\"},{\"title\":\"0.8.0 issue with Authentication · Issue #934 · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/934\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/doc/feature-matrix.md at master · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/doc/feature-matrix.md\"},{\"title\":\"Git-bug: Part 1 - Fresh/Brewed\",\"url\":\"https://freshbrewed.science/2022/12/09/gitbug.html\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug - Open Collective\",\"url\":\"https://opencollective.com/git-bug\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/git-bug | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/git-bug/git-bug\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about git-bug's entity DAG framework and related components:\n\n## Entity Package and DAG Framework\n\nThe entity package is capable of handling complex operations of an Entity (bug, board, config): operations, DAG manipulation, conflict merge, signature, integrity. Writing new entities (configuration, pull-request, board) becomes nearly as simple as for a CRUD application.\n\n## Key Technical Features\n\nOperations can now be represented in a DAG with concurrent editions across machines while still supporting proper merge conflict, instead of the enforced linear structure as before.\n\nThe framework includes several important concepts:\n\n- **Operation-based Architecture**: Entities (bugs, identities) are defined by a sequence of operations rather than their final state that, when applied in sequence, compute the current state of the bug.\n\n- **Identifiers**: CombinedId is a new kind of identifier for an item within an Entity (for example a comment in a bug), that holds two partial identifiers interleaved for fast addressing.\n\n- **Entity Linking**: The concept of resolvers allows entities to link to another.\n\n## Related Components\n\nGit-bug includes a robust identity system that allows users to create and manage their digital identities within the system, which are used to attribute bug operations and establish authorship.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","type":"input_text"}],"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HVkqA67uBWTpuejSasWCDG","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"tool_result"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"6db8b27b11f6bb207423cc2df7e9f08e7dfe6cdb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-c058bfa5e8718c63b0b8ccbab4a59e1faae994dce43db07da07c63f440f890de","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-07T23:17:16.654Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"call_id":"toolu_01HVkqA67uBWTpuejSasWCDG","output":[{"text":"Web search results for query: \"git-bug entity dag framework used for Bug Identity Board entities \"entity\" package what else\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Release 0.8.0 · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases/tag/v0.8.0\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/entity/dag/example_test.go at master · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/entity/dag/example_test.go\"},{\"title\":\"Pull requests · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/pulls\"},{\"title\":\"0.8.0 issue with Authentication · Issue #934 · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/934\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/doc/feature-matrix.md at master · git-bug/git-bug\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/doc/feature-matrix.md\"},{\"title\":\"Git-bug: Part 1 - Fresh/Brewed\",\"url\":\"https://freshbrewed.science/2022/12/09/gitbug.html\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug - Open Collective\",\"url\":\"https://opencollective.com/git-bug\"},{\"title\":\"git-bug/git-bug | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/git-bug/git-bug\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about git-bug's entity DAG framework and related components:\n\n## Entity Package and DAG Framework\n\nThe entity package is capable of handling complex operations of an Entity (bug, board, config): operations, DAG manipulation, conflict merge, signature, integrity. Writing new entities (configuration, pull-request, board) becomes nearly as simple as for a CRUD application.\n\n## Key Technical Features\n\nOperations can now be represented in a DAG with concurrent editions across machines while still supporting proper merge conflict, instead of the enforced linear structure as before.\n\nThe framework includes several important concepts:\n\n- **Operation-based Architecture**: Entities (bugs, identities) are defined by a sequence of operations rather than their final state that, when applied in sequence, compute the current state of the bug.\n\n- **Identifiers**: CombinedId is a new kind of identifier for an item within an Entity (for example a comment in a bug), that holds two partial identifiers interleaved for fast addressing.\n\n- **Entity Linking**: The concept of resolvers allows entities to link to another.\n\n## Related Components\n\nGit-bug includes a robust identity system that allows users to create and manage their digital identities within the system, which are used to attribute bug operations and establish authorship.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.","type":"input_text"}],"type":"function_call_output"},"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:17:16.654Z","type":"response_item"},"format":"codex-rollout-jsonl/2"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-23T23:00:35.198Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"codex:331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","seq":617}}
