{"content":{"blocks":[{"id":"toolu_01K5jaFVcej6rRZanmpKEiQD","input":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: project-annals-extraction\\ndescription: annals package extracted from cledger (2026-09-01) — store layer as content-agnostic git-notes record library; cledger 0.26.0 sits on it; ev1 history to be wiped, not migrated\\nmetadata:\\n  type: project\\n---\\n\\n2026-09-01: extracted cledger's storage layer into a new sibling package\\n**`annals`** (`~/repos/evintunador/annals`, name confirmed free on npm; user\\npicked it over git-ledger). Grew out of reviewing the (retired)\\n`design/extension-governance` branch: rather than governing third-party\\nkinds inside cledger, the store became its own layer and vocabularies\\nvalidate themselves.\\n\\nKey decisions:\\n- Envelope: schema `annals/v1`, ids `ev2-`, `conversation` renamed\\n  **`stream`** ({id, seq, parent}); `actor` kept in the envelope as generic\\n  attribution; content never interpreted. Third-party kinds identified by\\n  `(producer.tool, kind)`; the store validates the envelope only — no\\n  registry (Decision 4 of the old governance doc dissolved).\\n- **Namespaces**: every op takes a `Ledger` (RepoInfo + NamespaceConfig)\\n  from `openLedger()`; a namespace picks notes ref, state dir, config file,\\n  cliName, and the pre-push hook invocation. cledger's namespace keeps all\\n  old names (refs/notes/conversation-ledger, .cledger.json, ~/.config/\\n  cledger). Separate refs are for future producers ([[project-ledger-ecosystem]]:\\n  intent-recall wants its own wipeable ref per its D13).\\n- ReadOptions gained `tool`, `kind: string|string[]`, `linkRel`;\\n  `conversation` filter renamed `stream`.\\n- cledger 0.26.0 keeps its old module paths as thin namespace-binding\\n  wrappers, so turnbridge's import surface survived; `ConversationRef`\\n  stays exported as an alias of `StreamRef`.\\n- **No migration**: user chose wiping ev1 history over rewriting (sole\\n  user). `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh` in conversation-ledger (dry-run\\n  default) — the human runs `--execute`; agents must not.\\n\\nState: local branches only, nothing pushed — annals repo `main` (no remote\\nyet), conversation-ledger `annals-extraction`, turnbridge `annals-cledger`.\\nTests: annals 150, cledger 90, turnbridge 91, all green. cledger/turnbridge\\nstay separate packages: turnbridge → cledger → annals is one-way, and\\ncontext-graph/intent-recall want conversations without fabrication\\nmachinery. annals CLI is minimal (sync, transport-push) by design.\\n\",\"file_path\":\"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-annals-extraction.md\"}","name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"6db8b27b11f6bb207423cc2df7e9f08e7dfe6cdb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-b7b89a4584f2128a4114afb39dcac8f262f8b182f29751e95937a8f2b01bde30","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-01T22:57:03.771Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"arguments":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: project-annals-extraction\\ndescription: annals package extracted from cledger (2026-09-01) — store layer as content-agnostic git-notes record library; cledger 0.26.0 sits on it; ev1 history to be wiped, not migrated\\nmetadata:\\n  type: project\\n---\\n\\n2026-09-01: extracted cledger's storage layer into a new sibling package\\n**`annals`** (`~/repos/evintunador/annals`, name confirmed free on npm; user\\npicked it over git-ledger). Grew out of reviewing the (retired)\\n`design/extension-governance` branch: rather than governing third-party\\nkinds inside cledger, the store became its own layer and v