r extension-governance handoff shipped in different form: the\nregistration/discovery mechanism was deliberately NOT built. The contract\nis: a third-party kind is identified by (producer.tool, kind); whoever emits\na vocabulary publishes its reader — for `continuation` that reader is\nturnbridge's own readLineage/ContinuationRecord export, which context-graph\nwill import rather than parsing content by hand. Rewrite section A as a\nshort pointer to annals' README and this contract.\n\nStep 3 — work section B of docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md, which stays entirely in\nthis repo. Suggested order, cheap to deep:\n  a. Read producer.model / producer.provider instead of actor.id for model\n     identity (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md §1). opencode.ts:217-221 currently\n     guesses provider by string-splitting the model id; producer.provider is\n     the stated answer, and unset means \"source didn't say\", never infer.\n  b. Marker reduction (POLICY_SPLIT.md §4): opencode's reasoning parts are\n     plaintext, so stop injecting `[visible thinking]` on the opencode path —\n     emit a native reasoning part. Claude/Codex paths cannot change.\n  c. Move human-facing disclosures (model substitution, ancestor\n     unavailable, size) out of the fabricated transcript into plan.notes;\n     only the import notice belongs in model context.\n  d. Probe whether Claude's system/attachment lines reach model context\n     (docs/specs/claude-session-format.md:74,:196 disagree with cledger's\n     context_injection framing); if they do, the import notice can stop\n     being a counterfeit user turn.\n  e. The big one — multi-hop re-sourcing (LINEAGE §2-3a): when bridging a\n     conversation whose prefix is itself an import, walk parentOf\n     transitively and render each turn from the conversation where it\n     ORIGINATED, never from a copy (\"copy from the original, never from the\n     previous copy\"). Prerequisite: record the ordered source event ids in\n     the continuation event's content at fabricate time (content is\n     turnbridge-owned; no cledger change needed). Decisions already leaning\n     but to be confirmed as you go: render \"as it would have been\" (undo\n     turnbridge's own transport damage, don't invent history); degrade\n     gracefully to the copy when the ancestor is unreachable, with\n     disclosure; collapse ancestral import notices into one that names the\n     whole chain.\n\nHouse rules: this repo is PUBLIC and this conversation is captured by\ncledger into git notes that also get pushed. Never type a whole\nformat-valid credential (real or fake) into code, docs, commit messages, or\nchat — keyword-shaped fakes need an uppercase FAKE/EXAMPLE/TESTONLY marker\ninside the value, and format-valid test tokens must be stored split so that\nNO individual fragment is matchable by a public secret scanner on its own\n(a Slack-shaped fragment in a fixture just fired a GitGuardian alert for\nexactly this). If the pre-push scan reports findings, stop and hand the\nqueue to the human; do not read flagged content into the session.\n```\n\nTwo notes on it: step 0 has the agent push the branch itself (it's still local-only here), and I left PR-#11-merge out of its preconditions — the branch builds against cledger's `annals-extraction` via the `file:` link regardless of whether you've merged yet.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"6db8b27b11f6bb207423cc2df7e9f08e7dfe6cdb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-7696f719e0b6c62d1731f973158ef0d0d26e7caadc6eed2c87dedf37fb1b9b79","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-10T03:16:46.842Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload