{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All four answered — one of them turned up something you should know about immediately.\n\n## 4. Your live installs: **the new code is already live** — no action needed, but know it happened\n\nYour global `cledger` is an npm link resolving into the repo working directory (`/opt/homebrew/bin/cledger → …/conversation-ledger/dist/cli.js`, package linked to `~/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger`), and every hook (Claude Code, Codex, the opencode plugin, gemini/qwen) invokes `cledger` off PATH. The repo has been sitting on `annals-extraction` with the branch built since ~7:30pm — so every capture since then, including this session's, has been writing ev2/`annals/v1` events (your conversation-ledger notes ref was last written 3:02am tonight). So:\n\n- **Nothing to install.** cledger reaches annals through the `file:../annals` symlink; repo hooks upgrade themselves in place on the next append (smoke test 2 verified that path).\n- Your refs currently hold mixed ev1+ev2 events. Reads tolerate this (also verified), and the wipe script deletes the whole ref, both generations — so nothing to clean up separately.\n- Two cautions: don't `git checkout main` in conversation-ledger without rebuilding (stale branch `dist/` against main sources), so merging the branches soonish is the tidy move; and only run `npm link` in `~/repos/evintunador/annals` if you ever want the bare `annals` CLI — cledger doesn't need it.\n\n## 1. Envelope holdovers — one structural, several cosmetic\n\nHonest audit: **`actor` being *required* is the one real cledger assumption left.** Its human/agent/system trichotomy and \"git email or model id\" semantics are conversation vocabulary; a tunalab run record has no natural actor. I'd make it optional in the envelope (validate shape only when present, cledger keeps requiring it for its kinds) — cheap *now*, before any post-wipe data exists, and it doesn't change ids of events that carry one. The gray zone is `producer.model`/`provider`/`source_version` — AI-provenance riding in the envelope — but they're optional, identity-excluded, and power cross-vocabulary read filters, so I'd keep them and just reword their turn-centric doc comments. `resolved` and `stream.seq` are generic concepts with cledger-specific docs (cosmetic). `raw`, `links`, `context`, `media_type`, `redactions` are genuinely store-level. Say the word and I'll make actor optional + fix the docs.\n\n## 2. Size policy enforcement — in scope, but warn-only\n\nToday it's prose only; nothing checks. A hard cap is wrong on the capture path (cledger's \"capture must never fail\" rule — a huge pasted blob in a transcript should still be recorded), so the right shape is: an append-time guard in annals that warns once per repo when a serialized event crosses a threshold (say 512KB, configurable), with an opt-in strict mode that refuses for producers who want it (a derived layer can afford to fail loudly). ~30 lines plus a test. Worth doing before intent-recall/tunalab start writing; I'd hold the strict mode until a producer asks.\n\n## 3. What else git-bug built on its entity framework\n\nDirectly from their releases/docs: the `entity/dag` package runs **Bug** (issues — create/comment/label/status as operations), **Identity** (users themselves are git-stored, versioned, signable entities — the attribution layer is an entity like any other), and **Board** (kanban), with **config** and **pull-request** explicitly named as anticipated future entities (\"writing new entities… becomes nearly as simple as for a CRUD application\"). Two of their supporting concepts map straight onto annals: **resolvers** (entities linking to other entities — your `links`) and **CombinedId** (addressing an item *within* an entity, like a comment in a bug — your `stream` + `seq`). Their bridges (GitHub/GitLab/Jira sync) sit on top as import/export, not entities. The Identity-as-entity idea is the interesting one for you: if multi-user attribution ever matters (the turnbridge \"Alice and Bob\" scenario), git-bug's answer was to make identity a first-class record in the store rather than an envelope field.\n\nSources: [git-bug 0.8.0 release notes](https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases/tag/v0.8.0), [entity/dag example](https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/master/entity/dag/example_test.go), [git-bug releases](https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/releases)\n\nresult: Answered all four — your live install already runs the new code via the global npm link (captures have been writing ev2 events since tonight's build; wipe covers it, merge branches soon); the envelope's one real holdover is required-`actor` (recommend optional, cheap pre-wipe); size policy should get a warn-only append guard; git-bug's framework also ran Identity-as-entity and Board, with resolvers/CombinedId mirroring annals' links/stream+seq.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"6db8b27b11f6bb207423cc2df7e9f08e7dfe6cdb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-2a425f683fb65d5ca7fef2a580e5a0dd54083daec728896ac391da3fc6bbe988","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"331d6dd2-a7e9-4695-8b0e-9b329a3e5e00","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-07T23:18:13.368Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"content":[{"text":"All four answered — one of them turned up something you should know about immediately.\n\n## 4. Your live installs: **the new code is already live** — no action needed, but know it happened\n\nYour global `cledger` is an npm link resolving into the repo working directory (`/opt/homebrew/bin/cledger → …/conversation-ledger/dist/cli.js`, package linked to `~/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger`), and every hook (Claude Code, Codex, the openc